      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Blood platelet activity and levels of proteinase inhibitors and proteolytic components were assessed in patients with progressive angina of effort, spontaneous angina and acute myocardial infarction. alpha 1-antitrypsin and alpha 2-macroglobulin were shown to be involved in fibrinolysis regulation and kininogenesis. In acute myocardial infarction, there was a close inverse correlation between platelet release and blood kallikrein levels."},
